# Integration Guide — Document Service
 
**Who this is for:** anyone on the Resolve team connecting their service to
Document Service, or connecting Document Service to someone else's.
**What this is not:** a rewrite of the API contract. For exact request/
response shapes, see `Contracts/Document_Service.md`. This doc explains
*why* each connection exists and *what to actually do* about it.
 
---
 
## The one-paragraph mental model
 
Think of Document Service as a **hotel concierge who takes packages for
guests**. Before accepting a package, the concierge needs:
 
- **The front desk** (Authentication) to confirm the person really is a
  guest, not a stranger off the street.
- **Security** (RBAC) to confirm this guest is actually allowed to receive
  packages — maybe some guests have that privilege revoked.
- **The reservation system** (Case Management) to confirm the room number
  they gave is real.
- **The hotel manager's office** (Organization Service) to confirm the
  whole hotel branch they're staying at hasn't been shut down.
Once the package is accepted, the concierge doesn't personally deliver it to
every interested party — they just **announce it on the intercom**
(Kafka), and whichever departments care (housekeeping, security, the mail
room) pick it up on their own time.
 
---
 
## Who connects to Document Service, and in which direction
 
| Other service | Direction | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **Authentication** (Task 4) | Document Service **depends on it** | Needs to know who's calling and from which tenant |
| **RBAC** (Task 5) | Document Service **depends on it** | Needs to know if that caller is allowed to upload/read |
| **Case Management** (Task 6) | Document Service **depends on it** | A document always attaches to a case that has to actually exist |
| **Organization Service** (Task 2) | Document Service **depends on it** | A suspended tenant shouldn't be able to upload new documents |
| **Audit, Virus Scanner, OCR Worker, Metadata Processor, Search Indexer** | They **depend on Document Service** | They all react to the `DocumentUploaded` Kafka event, each for their own reason |
 
Document Service is almost entirely a **consumer** of other services for its
synchronous checks, and a **producer** for everyone downstream via Kafka. It
never calls Audit, the scanner, or the search indexer directly — it just
publishes an event and lets them come to it.
 
---
 
## The stub pattern — why integration here is low-risk
 
Every one of Document Service's four upstream dependencies is currently
answered by a tiny stand-in function that always says "yes." This was
deliberate, so the service could be built and tested before any of those
four other services existed. Each stand-in lives in exactly one file:
 
| Dependency | File | Current behavior |
|---|---|---|
| Authentication | `src/middleware/auth.js` | Fakes one hardcoded user for every request |
| RBAC | `src/services/permissionClient.js` | Always returns `true` |
| Case Management | `src/services/caseClient.js` | Always confirms the case exists |
| Organization | *not built yet — see below* | No check happens at all |
 
**What this means for integration:** going live with any one of these is an
edit to one file, not a rewrite of the service. Nothing in the routes,
controllers, database code, or Kafka logic needs to change.
 
