## Connection 4 — Organization Service (Task 2)
 
**Plain words:** if a whole tenant's account gets suspended, nobody there
should be able to upload new files, even if their login still technically
works.
 
**The honest status:** this is the one connection that isn't even stubbed
yet — not "fake until real," genuinely missing. Worth building the stub
now, before the real service exists, following the exact same pattern as
the other three:
 
```javascript
// src/services/organizationClient.js
async function assertOrganizationActive(tenantId)
{
    return true; // placeholder — replace with a call to
                 // GET /internal/v1/organizations/{id} once reachable,
                 // and reject with 403 if status !== "ACTIVE"
}
 
module.exports = { assertOrganizationActive };
```
Call it once per write (upload, new version) — not on reads, matching the
rule Organization Service's own contract lays out for every other service.
 
